// PARKED KNOWN-OPEN DIVERGENCE (aug05h ryouko reactive divergence_000000;
// fix 6fcd6c1e REVERTED same night after it flooded 48 findings/hour).
// Needs a DESIGNED fix and probably Eric's ruling on the interp rule
// itself. Current behavior: the JIT MISSES a re-fire the interp emits
// (rarer, safer direction: ~1 finding per 7M reactive subjects).
//
// THE INTERP RULE, as measured (all probed on a568122c):
// - scrutinee fires, selected arm produces a value -> emit.
// - scrutinee fires, arm body QUIET/STARVED (a fold whose callback
//   capture never fired; a const arm after init) -> RE-EMIT the arm's
//   ridden value, FIRED (sb1/sb2 probes: one emission per injection
//   epoch, both pattern kinds, both modes agree on const arms).
// - scrutinee fires, arm body EVALUATES to bottom (div0: delivered
//   interior taint) -> SILENT, no ride (the aug05i flood witnesses:
//   interp emits nothing at the injection cycle).
//
// WHY THE KERNEL CAN'T CURRENTLY MATCH: both "arm starved" and "arm
// evaluated-bottom" reach the fused select's merge as identical
// TAINT|STALE discs (propagate_flags forces TAINT=>STALE, erasing
// provenance). The merge taint-cache substitutes the ride with
// disc=clean|STALE, and the output freshness gate swallows it — so
// the STARVED case misses its re-fire (this witness). The reverted
// fix ANDed the scrutinee's STALE into the merged disc, which fired
// the ride for BOTH cases — the EVALUATED-bottom case then over-fired
// (48 findings in one hour across the fleet, all the same class:
// jit emits the ridden value at injection cycles where the interp is
// silent because the taken arm div0s).
//
// A correct fix needs the absence-vs-evaluated-bottom distinction to
// survive to the merge (a provenance bit, or absence handled
// structurally before the body computes). Same provenance gap killed
// the emit_fold_loop absent-capture guard drafted earlier the same
// night. Diagnosis kit: GRAPHIX_DBG_REGION (what fused + input
// wiring), GXDBG_KPOLL (per-kernel polls with fired/present),
// sb1/sb2-style minimal probes in the aug05 scratchpad.
//
// This witness: jit misses the epoch-2 injection-cycle re-emit
// (interp [0:2];[0:2], jit [0:2];[]).
// schedule-v1: cap=80 events=640; in0=i64:1
{let v0: Array<i64> = []; v0 <- in0 ~ array::push(v0, in0); let v8 = |v9: i64| select v9 {i64:0 => (i64:1 + v9), _ => error(true)}; let v10 = (try (v8(i64:1))? catch(e) => (-(in0))); let v11: i64 = select in0 {v11 => array::fold(v0, i64:2, |v12, x| v10)}; v11}
